---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { OFFICIAL, CONTACT_EMAIL, LAST_UPDATED } from '../data/site';

const path = '/about/';
const title = 'About Astrae Oratio Wiki: Sources, Editorial Policy & Corrections';
const description =
  'About this unofficial Astrae Oratio fan wiki: how we source information, how CBT and press details are labeled, our use of official material, and how to report corrections.';
---

<Base
  {title}
  {description}
  {path}
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
    { name: 'About', href: path },
  ]}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="prose">
      <header class="page-head">
        <p class="kicker">About</p>
        <h1>About this wiki</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          Astrae Oratio Wiki (astraeoratio.org) is an <strong>unofficial, fan-made</strong> guide to Astrae Oratio. It is not
          affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored by NC Corporation or Dynamis One.
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="callout warn">
        <span class="callout-title">Looking for the official site?</span>
        The official Astrae Oratio website is <a href={OFFICIAL.site} rel="noopener">astraeoratio.plaync.com</a>. Account,
        payment and support questions should go to <a href={OFFICIAL.support} rel="noopener">NC customer support</a> — we can’t
        help with those.
      </div>

      <h2 id="sources">How we source information</h2>
      <p>Every page lists its sources at the bottom. In order of preference, we use:</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Official material</strong> — the official website (all four languages), official notices and the official social accounts.</li>
        <li><strong>Established press</strong> — outlets such as Inven Global, Gematsu and AUTOMATON, especially for interviews and event coverage.</li>
        <li><strong>Hands-on footage and player reports</strong> — used for systems that only appeared in the closed beta, and always labeled as such.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Because Astrae Oratio has not launched, a lot of information comes from the October 2026 CBT. Those details are marked
        as <strong>CBT</strong> information and may change. We don’t publish leaks, datamined content or rumors as fact.
      </p>

      <h2 id="names">Names and spellings</h2>
      <p>
        Character and term names follow the <strong>official English website</strong>, with Japanese names from the official
        Japanese site. For characters without an official profile yet, we use the spelling shown in the CBT’s English build and
        say so on the page.
      </p>

      <h2 id="assets">Official material and fan policy</h2>
      <p>
        We write our own summaries instead of copying official text, and we don’t host official artwork. Character pages use
        original “star sign” graphics generated for this site. Official trailers are embedded directly from the official
        YouTube channels. We follow the spirit of the official
        <a href={OFFICIAL.fanPolicy} rel="noopener">fan content guidelines</a>; if a rights holder would like something
        changed, please contact us and we’ll act promptly.
      </p>

      <h2 id="corrections">Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        Found a mistake, a missing source or something out of date? Email <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
        with the page URL and, ideally, a link to the source. We correct factual errors as soon as we can verify them and
        update the page’s date.
      </p>

      <h2 id="trademarks">Trademarks</h2>
      <p>
        Astrae Oratio and all related names, characters and images are trademarks or copyrighted material of Dynamis One,
        licensed to NC Corporation. They are used here for identification and commentary only.
      </p>

      <p class="meta-line">Last updated <time datetime={LAST_UPDATED}>{LAST_UPDATED}</time></p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
